      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{62770b2ab9aa4552a0459dc1|full_name} Proton is not viable without programs like Envision to fix reprojection and gain sufficient performance. SteamVR itself has fixed it's own issues for the most part but running VRChat through Proton via SteamVR is NOT VIABLE, It has major reprojection issues, it's like having serious double vision constantly. -And while yes, Envision exists, it's fragile and can break at any point. \n\nAs for shaders, Vulkan has the capability to compile shaders from any platform but of course 3rd party shaders like Poiyomi, liltoon, and UTS2 might make DX11 calls, which would be the main issue. \n\nIf that's the case, the best option would be to use DXVK to translate DX11 calls but I'm not sure how this could be implemented properly.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
